---
// https://mateu.io/privacy — the privacy policy of the Mateu apps (the phone app in the App Store and
// Google Play, the sideloaded Android APK and the desktop app). Both stores require a privacy policy
// URL even for an app that collects nothing. Its substance is frontend/app/react-native/RELEASE.md
// §5 (the store privacy answers): keep the two in step.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
	<title>Privacy policy — Mateu apps</title>
	<meta name="description" content="What the Mateu phone and desktop apps do with your data: they collect nothing." />
	<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" />
	<style>
		:root { --bg: #f6f7f9; --card: #ffffff; --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: #5b6270; --line: #d9dde3; --accent: #1f6feb; }
		@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
			:root { --bg: #111418; --card: #1b1f25; --ink: #eceff3; --muted: #a3abb8; --line: #333a44; --accent: #5b9bff; }
		}
		* { box-sizing: border-box; }
		body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; }
		main { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 16px 3rem; }
		.card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; }
		h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
		h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; }
		p, li { margin: .5rem 0; }
		ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
		.muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
		.summary { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: .25rem 0 .25rem 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
		a { color: var(--accent); }
		a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
		footer { margin-top: 1.5rem; text-align: center; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<main>
		<article class="card">
			<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="muted">The Mateu apps: Mateu for iPhone and Android, and the Mateu desktop app. Last updated: 31 October 2026.</p>

			<p class="summary"><strong>In short: the Mateu apps collect no data.</strong> There is no Mateu
			account, no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising and no tracking. What you type into an
			application you open goes to that application's own server, never to us.</p>

			<h2>What the apps are</h2>
			<p>Mateu is a client for business applications built with the open-source
			<a href="https://mateu.io">Mateu</a> framework. Organisations run those applications on their own
			servers. You add one to the app by scanning its QR code, opening its link or typing its address,
			and the app shows its screens.</p>

			<h2>What we collect</h2>
			<p>Nothing. The publisher of the Mateu apps runs no server the apps report to, and receives no data
			about you or about how you use the apps.</p>

			<h2>The applications you open</h2>
			<p>Each application you add belongs to the organisation that publishes it, which receives what you
			enter in it and is responsible for that data under its own privacy policy. The app talks to each
			application's server only over encrypted connections (HTTPS). If an application asks you to sign
			in, you do so with that organisation's identity provider, in the system browser: the app never
			sees your password.</p>

			<h2>What stays on your device</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Your list of applications: their addresses, names and icons.</li>
				<li>For each application, its sign-in tokens and a random session identifier, kept in the
				device's secure storage (the Keychain on iPhone and Mac, the Android Keystore, the operating
				system's credential store on the desktop).</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Removing an application from your list deletes what the app stored for it; uninstalling the app
			deletes everything. The "Export my UIs" code carries the addresses only — never sign-ins.</p>

			<h2>Permissions</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Camera</strong> (phone): to scan QR codes, and for photo fields an application asks
				you to fill in. Nothing is recorded or sent anywhere except the photo you choose to submit to
				that application.</li>
				<li><strong>Screen</strong> (desktop, only when you ask it to read a QR code from your screen):
				the capture is read on your computer and discarded.</li>
				<li><strong>Internet</strong>: to reach the applications you add. The desktop app also checks
				GitHub for its own updates.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>The apps are business tools and are not directed at children.</p>

			<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
			<p>Changes to this policy are published on this page. Questions:
			<a href="https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/issues">github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/issues</a>.</p>
			<p class="muted">Publisher: Miguel Pérez Colom.</p>
		</article>
		<footer><a href="/">mateu.io</a></footer>
	</main>
</body>
</html>
